From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Robinson <mrobinson@igalia.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:36:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: deny: Accept unmaintained zbus-related crates
 (#48994)

Our dependencies are still using zbus on main.
Accept the unmaintained status.

--------

We must accept these until our dependencies stop using them. In
particular these are used by `atspi-common`.

Testing: This should unblock the CI.

Signed-off-by: Martin Robinson <mrobinson@abandonedwig.info>
(cherry picked from commit 493d293e1947f8ebd9aed0b34c0393f0079838ef)

----

Fork note: backported onto Servo v0.6.0 for the ohos-v0.6 branch. A commit of upstream's release/v0.6 branch after v0.6.0, taken unchanged so that the next v0.6.x release supersedes it: v0.6.0's lock file fails cargo-deny in test-tidy. The subject drops the backticks around zbus, which the stack manifest's entry format doesn't allow.

Validation: On the final stack, at its tip: `./mach test-tidy` (including cargo-deny), `./mach test-scripts`, `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, the crown build (checked-release, -D warnings, crown built for Rust 1.97.1), `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` with and without `--doc`, and the OpenHarmony checked-release builds of both flavors with -D warnings, which make signed HAPs, pass; release builds of it with both engines ran the whole WPT suite. cargo-deny passes at the stack's tip, where plain v0.6.0 has 24 findings.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit 17153943cac without code changes and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 deny.toml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/deny.toml b/deny.toml
index c19d818d6a7..d116a9f02b0 100644
--- a/deny.toml
+++ b/deny.toml
@@ -40,6 +40,15 @@ ignore = [
     # This is a dependency of `usvg`, `rustybuzz`, `fontdb`.
     # We will need to wait for upstream actions.
     "RUSTSEC-2026-0192",
+    # The crate `zvariant` is unmaintained. Wait for `atspi-common` to start
+    # using `zbus`.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0370",
+    # The crate `zbus_names` is unmaintained. Wait for `atspi-common` to start
+    # using `zbus`.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0371",
+    # The crate `zvariant_derive` is unmaintained. Wait for `atspi-common` to start
+    # using `zbus`.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0372",
 ]
 
